        "user_title": null,
        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "<p>yeah, i noticed it. Didn&#39;t know the name for that &quot;letter spacing thing&quot;. Still it&#39;s because each letter has their own fixed width and they are not overlapping. The letters look crowded so it would look better if the top part of the T was above the low part of the L but from a... erm... &iquest;techincal? point of view it&#39;s not really flawed, just doesn&#39;t look right as it could.</p>",
