        "created_at": "2013-08-27T17:41:49.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Yes, that's why it happens, but good typography does still adjust things to make the letters overlap a little. &nbsp;One canonical example is VA; it looks much better if you let the letters overlap. &nbsp;The Wikipedia article looks pretty good on this:&nbsp;http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kerning</p>",
